									'text' => 'For a manufacturer, furniture product design is the process of turning a concept into a buildable, sellable product: proportions and dimensions, construction logic, material specification, template and BOM-related outputs, costing inputs and prototype refinement. It ends when the factory can produce the model repeatedly at a known cost and quality.',
